From 24c5ab47e0b54bd31cf3bd377bf50ce86c670933 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotsunchip <hotsunchip@kaist.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 20:06:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Pin note code-block copy button and refine code styling

The copy button was a child of the horizontally-scrolling <pre>, so a
long code line scrolled it out of view. Wrap the fenced block in a
non-scrolling .note-code-wrapper and make the button a sibling of the
<pre> (wrapper owns positioning, <pre> owns overflow) so it stays pinned.

Also refine code styling in the preview: drop the forced transparent
background from the shared .hljs rule, give inline code a neutral pill,
cancel the prose backtick pseudo-elements markdown-it makes redundant,
and add fenced-block backgrounds + a thin scrollbar (light and dark).

Local verify:fast is unreliable on this WSL/jsdom host (vitest fork
workers time out on random unrelated files); notes typecheck + the
preview suite pass. CI is the authoritative gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
